cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Chain-of-Thought Faithfulness Verification
message: "If you use this code, corpus, or methodology, please cite as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Charara
    given-names: Talia
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # fill in if applicable
    # affiliation: ""                                  # fill in if applicable
repository-code: "https://github.com/thcharara/cot-faithfulness"
abstract: >
  A multi-method framework for verifying whether large language models
  use their chain-of-thought reasoning, combining behavioural taxonomy
  coding with mechanistic interpretability (linear probes and activation
  steering). Includes a corpus of 320 reasoning traces from
  DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Llama-8B on visual inductive reasoning (Zendo)
  tasks, a 9-category taxonomy of reasoning operations, 73,383
  auto-coded sentences via Claude Sonnet, trained linear probes at
  layers 0/10/20/31, and steering-vector interventions at layer 20
  across 22 conditions.
keywords:
  - chain-of-thought
  - cot-faithfulness
  - mechanistic-interpretability
  - linear-probes
  - activation-steering
  - reasoning
  - large-language-models
  - deepseek-r1
